<title>USA: Centerior Ohio nuke resumes full power.</title>
<headline>Centerior Ohio nuke resumes full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Centerior Energy Corp's 877 megawatt Davis Besse nuclear power unit resumed full power production today, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Friday in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Oak Harbor, Ohio, was operating at 40 percent power Thursday while conducting routine leak tests.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
